<%# app/views/home/_credit_card_row.html.erb — locals: category, summary
    The reserved card row, expanding into one line per statement due this month.
    Native <details>: the browser owns the toggle, the keyboard handling and the
    screen-reader semantics, so there is no JavaScript here. Collapsed state
    resets on navigation — each month opens collapsed, which is accepted.

    With nothing due there is no <details> at all, only the summary's content in
    a plain <div>: a zero row must offer no disclosure affordance. Both branches
    keep dom_id(category, :row) so budgets/create.turbo_stream.erb's replace
    still finds the row.

    KNOWN WART: the category-name link sits inside the <summary>, so some
    browsers toggle the details on the way out of the click. Invisible, because
    the page navigates. If it reads badly, move the toggle to its own element. %>
<% due = summary.statements_due %>
<% row_id = dom_id(category, :row) %>
<% if due.any? %>
  <details id="<%= row_id %>" class="p-3">
    <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer">
      <%= render "home/credit_card_summary", category:, summary: %>
    </summary>
    <ul class="mt-2 pl-4 text-sm divide-y">
      <% due.rows.each do |row| %>
        <li class="py-1 flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
          <%= link_to row.statement.card.name,
                card_statement_path(row.statement.card, row.statement),
                class: "text-blue-600 hover:underline" %>
          <span class="text-gray-500"><%= statement_due_label(row.statement) %></span>
          <span class="shrink-0"><%= brl(row.amount_cents) %></span>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </details>
<% else %>
  <div id="<%= row_id %>" class="p-3 flex items-center justify-between">
    <%= render "home/credit_card_summary", category:, summary: %>
  </div>
<% end %>
